  "term": "Stanford–Binet Intelligence Scale",
  "definition": "The Stanford–Binet Intelligence Scale is a standardized assessment of intelligence and cognitive abilities for children and adults. It measures fluid reasoning, knowledge, quantitative reasoning, visual-spatial processing, and working memory, using both verbal and nonverbal tasks to help evaluate people with deafness, limited English, or communication disorders.",
